<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Batoche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1885</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batoche">Batoche</a>, fought on 9–12 May 1885 in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a>, was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a>. Canadian troops under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-middleton">Frederick Middleton</a> overran the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> settlement held by the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gabriel-dumont">Gabriel Dumont</a>. Riel surrendered days later and was tried and hanged for treason in Regina in November 1885.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-batoche.jpg" alt="Battle of Batoche" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seargent Grundy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Batoche_Print_by_Seargent_Grundy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
